<item><title>ECOWAS gives Gambia election bodies US$480,000</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/ecowas-gives-gambia-election-bodies-us-480-000-c374e3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/ecowas-gives-gambia-election-bodies-us-480-000-c374e3/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>The electoral commission will use its share to train 8,851 polling staff ahead of the December 5 presidential election.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:01:32 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/ecowas-gives-gambia-election-bodies-us-480-000-c374e3/share.jpg" length="41047" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/ecowas-gives-gambia-election-bodies-us-480-000-c374e3/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Barrow campaign expects 300,000 supporters at Banjul return</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/barrow-campaign-expects-300-000-supporters-at-banjul-return-6b4e3f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/barrow-campaign-expects-300-000-supporters-at-banjul-return-6b4e3f/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>The president is due back in Banjul on Thursday after a tour that the campaign says drew supporters and defections to his party.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:28:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Touray pledges cost-of-living taskforce within 100 days if elected</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/touray-pledges-cost-of-living-taskforce-within-100-days-if-203cb4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/touray-pledges-cost-of-living-taskforce-within-100-days-if-203cb4/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>The independent candidate says the taskforce would review measures affecting essential-goods prices, alongside proposed constitutional and public-sector reforms.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:11:03 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gambia&apos;s opposition coalition vows to hold rally despite warnings</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambia-s-opposition-coalition-vows-to-hold-rally-despite-0e4b05/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/gm/gambia-s-opposition-coalition-vows-to-hold-rally-despite-0e4b05/</guid><category>Gambia</category><description>Ousainu Darboe, the UDP leader and coalition candidate, says the Boiram meeting will proceed under the timetable the electoral commission approved, after the Janjanbureh meeting.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:07:56 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" length="31578" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/gm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
